# SPARKLET: built the way the design mockup builds it, from
# UV blobs with box legs, a tail and cube eyes.
#
# Y is up, +Z is the front, one world unit is one map tile. The lowest
# vertex sits on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0, so
# the game places it by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which
# is what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. The mockup's own
# winding is the opposite convention, so every face here is reversed from
# the JavaScript it was ported from.
#
# Two swept back spikes and a lightning tail.
# About 1.80 units tall, 187 triangles.

mtllib sparklet.mtl

